OL,5,G1200 Private Passions
OL,6,     FMichael Berkeley's guest is the
OL,7,     Fformer Beatles hairdresser, Leslie
OL,8,     FCavendish.
OL,9,G1330 Music Map
OL,10,     FSara Mohr-Pietsch wends her way
OL,11,     Ftowards Brahms' melancholic late
OL,12,     Fmasterpiece. With swansongs from
OL,13,     FFaure and Mozart, there's also
OL,14,     Ftime for a spot of salon carousing
OL,15,     Fin Vienna.
OL,16,G1500 Music Matters: How to listen
OL,17,     F2/3. Conductor Sakari Oramo opens
OL,18,     Fa window into the art of attentive
OL,19,     Flistening. Today, Sakari takes us
OL,20,     Finside the listener's mind, and
OL,21,     Fexplores how context affects how
OL,22,     Fwe listen.
